# Security headers for the whole site (Netlify _headers syntax).
# CSP notes:
# - style-src needs 'unsafe-inline' because the UI is themed with runtime
#   inline `style={{...}}` attributes (dynamic per-theme colors) throughout
#   the app — there is no static stylesheet to hash/nonce against. This is a
#   real, common trade-off for this kind of app, not an oversight: locking
#   style-src down further would require rewriting all theming to CSS
#   variables/classes, a much bigger change outside this pass.
# - script-src has no 'unsafe-inline': the built app ships no inline <script>
#   (verified against the production build output), so this is fully strict.
# - connect-src/img-src allow *.supabase.co (REST, Auth, Storage, Realtime
#   over wss) since the project's Supabase URL is an env var, not fixed here.
# - connect-src also allows *.sentry.io and *.ingest.us/de.sentry.io for error
#   reporting — harmless if VITE_SENTRY_DSN is unset (initSentry() never runs,
#   so nothing ever actually calls out to these hosts).
# - Paddle.js overlay checkout needs several things allowed, all under
#   *.paddle.com: script-src (loading cdn.paddle.com/paddle/v2/paddle.js
#   itself), style-src (the checkout's own CSS, e.g.
#   sandbox-cdn.paddle.com/paddle/v2/assets/css/paddle.css — missed on the
#   first pass, which silently broke the checkout's layout), frame-src (the
#   actual payment-form iframe, e.g. buy.paddle.com / sandbox-buy.paddle.com),
#   img-src, and connect-src (Paddle.js's own API calls for price previews,
#   localization, etc.). Wildcarding *.paddle.com instead of listing each
#   subdomain individually, since Paddle uses several and the exact set isn't
#   publicly documented as a fixed list. static.cloudflareinsights.com is an
#   analytics beacon Paddle.js itself injects onto the parent page — harmless
#   to allow, blocking it doesn't break checkout but does spam the console.
# - worker-src allows blob: in addition to 'self' — Sentry's Session Replay
#   integration creates its encoding worker from a blob: URL, which 'self'
#   alone does not cover in Chrome's CSP worker-src matching.
/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=(self)
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' https://*.paddle.com https://static.cloudflareinsights.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com https://*.paddle.com; font-src 'self' https://fonts.gstatic.com; img-src 'self' data: https://images.pexels.com https://*.supabase.co https://*.paddle.com; connect-src 'self' https://*.supabase.co wss://*.supabase.co https://*.sentry.io https://*.ingest.sentry.io https://*.ingest.us.sentry.io https://*.ingest.de.sentry.io https://*.paddle.com; frame-src https://*.paddle.com; worker-src 'self' blob:; manifest-src 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; object-src 'none'

# Hashed build assets are immutable — safe to cache aggressively.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
